## Boundaries and population

Every city is computed on two boundaries [ADR 0004]:

- **LAU** is the city boundary: the Eurostat GISCO local administrative unit of 2024. It is the default. Where a city has no clean LAU polygon, the OSM administrative relation replaces it.
- **FUA** is the functional urban area, the city with its commuting zone. It is a robustness check.

Results are only compared within the same boundary kind. The LAU population comes from Eurostat. A city made of several LAU (`lau_codes`) has the sum of their figures, and only when every one has a figure. Where the LAU has no figure, the official population of the national statistics office, cited with year and URL in `config/cities.yaml` (`population_override`), supplies it. Without one, the identical NUTS3 unit supplies it [ADR 0004]. The code can also fall back to the Eurostat Urban Audit city population (`urb_cpop1`, set per city as `population_urau`), but no configured city uses it: the Urban Audit cities turned out to be greater cities, not the municipality [user decision on population of 2026-10-03, `docs/superpowers/rulings-m5.md`; `population` in `sources/boundaries.py`]. One population value applies to all snapshot years [M3 spec, decision 2]. FUA runs carry no population, so the FUA has no per-100k figure [M4 spec §4.4].

